# H.E.N.R.Y. Cursor Rules

## Documentation Policy

-   NEVER create new markdown documentation files unless explicitly requested
-   Update existing docs (CLAUDE.md, development-guide.md) instead of creating new ones
-   Prefer inline code comments and docstrings over separate documentation files
-   Keep explanations concise and focused

## Token Efficiency

-   Read only the specific files/sections needed, not entire directories
-   Use grep with targeted patterns instead of broad searches
-   Avoid reading large generated files (poetry.lock, **pycache**)
-   Batch related file reads in parallel when possible
-   Skip reading files when content can be inferred from context

## UI Development

-   All UI code uses pygame with 800x480 resolution (Raspberry Pi touchscreen)
-   ALWAYS verify scaling and positioning for the target resolution
-   Use relative positioning and scaling factors, never hardcoded pixel values
-   Test that text is readable at display size (min 20px font for body text)
-   Ensure touch targets are at least 44x44 pixels for usability
-   Check color contrast for readability (especially for small text)
-   Verify all UI elements fit within screen bounds before completing changes
-   Use ScreenManager (backend/services/screen_manager.py) as single source of truth for UI state

## Code Style & Architecture

-   Python 3.9-3.11 only (not 3.12+ due to tflite-runtime constraint)
-   Black formatting with 100 char line length
-   Use singleton pattern via `ServiceClass.get_instance()` for all services
-   All I/O operations must be async with sync wrappers for compatibility
-   Tools inherit from BaseTool and register with ToolsRegistry
-   Use Pydantic settings from backend/config/settings.py
-   Follow existing patterns in similar files rather than inventing new approaches

## Testing

-   Write tests for new features in tests/ directory
-   Use pytest fixtures for service instances
-   Mock external dependencies (Ollama, Neo4j, audio services)
-   Run tests before considering task complete

## Deployment Context

-   Development: local machine with .env.local
-   Production: Raspberry Pi with .env.pi
-   Consider resource constraints (RPi 4 with 4GB RAM)
-   Use quantized models and efficient algorithms

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

-   Don't use Python 3.12+ features or dependencies
-   Don't forget async/sync wrapper pattern for services
-   Don't hardcode paths (use settings or relative paths)
-   Don't skip service initialization checks
-   Don't create redundant documentation files
-   Don't make UI changes without verifying on target resolution
